refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.parameters;
hostname
The hostname of the SNMP agent (server), optionally followed by a port, as in 127.0.0.1:161.
security_name
&snmp.parameter.security-name;
security_level
&snmp.parameter.security-level;
auth_protocol
&snmp.parameter.auth-protocol;
auth_passphrase
&snmp.parameter.auth-passphrase;
privacy_protocol
&snmp.parameter.privacy-protocol;
privacy_passphrase
&snmp.parameter.privacy-passphrase;
object_id
The root of the subtree to read: all the SNMP objects below object_id are returned. An empty string stands for .1.3.6.1.2.1 (mib-2), which is only a part of the whole tree. &null; does the same, but is deprecated.
An array with a single element is accepted. An array with several elements is not, as a walk reads a single subtree: an E_WARNING is emitted and &false; is returned.
timeout
The number of microseconds until the first timeout. The default, -1, selects the Net-SNMP library default: the timeout and retries settings of snmp.conf if present, otherwise one second and 5 retries.
retries
The number of times to retry if timeouts occur. The default, -1, selects the Net-SNMP library default, see timeout.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns an array of SNMP object values starting from the object_id as root or &false; on error.
The array is a list indexed from 0. &false; is returned, with an E_WARNING, if the subtree does not exist or is empty, for example "No Such Object" or "No more variables left in this MIB View". It is also returned on an error or a timeout during the walk, in which case the entries already received are discarded.

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws a ValueError if hostname contains a null byte,
 is 128 bytes long or longer, or has a port outside the range 0 to 65535,
 if security_name is empty or contains a null byte,
 if security_level, auth_protocol or privacy_protocol is not valid,
 if timeout is lower than -1,
 if retries is lower than -1 or too large,
 or if object_id is an empty array.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     Now throws a ValueError when the hostname
     length is equal to or greater than 128 bytes, when the port is
     negative or greater than 65535, or when the timeout or retries values
     are lower than -1 or too large.


   &snmp.changelog.privacy-protocol-aes;
   &snmp.changelog.auth-protocol-sha2;
